# Masquerade: Masquerading as resource-owner Drops Some Privileges

## Tags

* type: bug
* status: open
* priority: high
* assigned: fredm, zachs, acenteno
* keywords: gn2, genenetwork2, auth, gn-auth

## Description

* Go to https://genenetwork.org/
* Log in using one of the system-administrator users
* Go to the "View Dashboard" page
* Select "Masquerade As"
* Select a user who has a 'resource-owner' privilege but is not a system-administrator
* Click the "Masquerade" button to masquerade as that user
* Now go to the user's dashboard
* Go to "Data and Access Management" page
* Click on one of the resources that the user is 'resource-owner' on
* Scroll down to the "Resource Data" section
* Select the "Users" tab
* See errors like:
  ```
  Users:   UNAUTHORIZED: AuthorisationError ; You do not have the appropriate privileges to list users.
  ```

This bug is weird, in that it does not uniformly show up for all cases.
